Your model is still incomplete. Consider the likelihood that y11=0 and y12=0. That likelihood is 1−π1+π1(1−p11)(1−p12)=1−p11π1−p12π1+p11p12π1. If you multiply the associated two likelihoods that you present in CrossValidated <https://stats.stackexchange.com/questions/441829/hierarchical-model-does-leaving-out-a-latent-variable-hierarchy-level-result?noredirect=1#comment822674_441829>, you don't get that result. How does your description obtain the correct result?  Answer:  It doesn't address that.  Again, your approach to avoid a mention of a latent variable is not necessarily wrong. It is just incomplete.

What you need to do is show the likelihood for the resulting visit status for all visits at a single site rather than just for a particular visit at a particular site.  (Then one makes the assumption of independence of sites.)

Jim

